{"name":"Golden West","hex":"#e9ca94","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Golden West","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Nickname for California: a state of the United States."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A rural municipality in south-east Saskatchewan, Canada; in full, the Rural Municipality of Golden West No. 95."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Golden_West"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rural Municipality of Golden West No. 95","blocks":[{"text":"The Rural Municipality of Golden West No. 95 is a rural municipality (RM) in the Canadian province of Saskatchewan within Census Division No. 1 and SARM Division No. 1. It is located in the southeast portion of the province."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Moose_Mountain_Lake_01.jpg/330px-Moose_Mountain_Lake_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rural_Municipality_of_Golden_West_No._95","wikidata":"Q5579971"},{"title":"Golden West Airlines","blocks":[{"text":"Golden West Airlines was a commuter airline that operated flights on a high volume schedule in California. It ceased operations in 1983."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c8/Logoname-golden-west-airlines-1980s.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_West_Airlines","wikidata":"Q5579957"},{"title":"Golden West (clipper)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden West was an 1852 extreme clipper built by Paul Curtis. The ship had a very active career in the California trade, the guano trade, the coolie trade, the Far East, and Australia. She made a record passage between Japan and San Francisco in 1856."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Clipper_Ship_Golden_West%2C_Outward_Bound_1852_3m08.jpg/330px-Clipper_Ship_Golden_West%2C_Outward_Bound_1852_3m08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped